{
  "id": "ior",
  "term": "IOR",
  "definition": "IOR, or inhibition of return, is an attention effect seen in spatial cueing tasks where, after a short delay, people become slower to respond to a target appearing in a previously cued location than to one appearing elsewhere. It reflects a shift from early attention toward the cue to later reduced efficiency for returning attention there, which may help favor new locations during visual search.",
